      "@type": "akn:paragraph",
      "eli:number": "b",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1992/41/eng@/~cl_6",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "by substituting for subsection (1) the following new subsection (1): \"(1) Where— (a) the Registrar is satisfied that any person who is registered under this Act is admitted to or confined in a mental hospital under the provisions of any law; MEDICAL (AMENDMENT) (b) any person who is registered under this Act has been certified by a medical review panel, which shall consist of not less than three medical practitioners appointed by the Council, to be unfit to perform his professional duty by reason of his mental or physical condition, he shall thereupon cease to be so registered, and an endorsement shall accordingly be made against his name in the Register.\"; and"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1992/41/eng@/~cl_6__para_c",
      "@type": "akn:paragraph",
      "eli:number": "c",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1992/41/eng@/~cl_6",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "by substituting for the words \"mental condition\" appearing in subsection (2) the words \"mental or physical condition, as the case may be,\"."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1992/41/eng@/~cl_7",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "7",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1992/41/eng@",
      "schema:name": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The principal Act is amended by inserting"
      },
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "immediately after section 34B the following new section 34c. (1) The Director General may authorise in writing any medical practitioner who is fully registered under section 14 and not being a medical practitioner in the public service to undertake any of the following functions, that is— (a) investigation, examination, treatment or management of any patient; or (b) perform an autopsy or post-mortem investigation of any deceased person, in any hospital, clinic or health centre or in any other similar institution. (2) A medical practitioner who is so authorised under subsection (1) to perform any of the functions referred to in paragraphs (a) and (b) thereof shall be deemed to be a Government Medical Officer for the purposes of the Criminal Procedure Code and any other relevant laws in Malaysia.\". BILL"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1992/41/eng@/~cl_8",
